#: .\templates\home\index.html:65
msgid "PolyQ Database"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:66
msgid ""
"A website with information regarding the 9 polyglutamine diseases documented "
"so far."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:72 .\templates\home\index.html:183
msgid "Huntington's Disease"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:73
msgid ""
"Huntington's Disease is the most widely studied and the most well known "
"polyglutamine disease. When it comes to neurodegenerative diseases, HD is "
"the most common inherited across generations and is mainly characterized by "
"excessive and uncontrolled motor movements."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:83
msgid "Dentatorubral pallidoluysian atrophy"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:84
msgid ""
"Dentatorubral pallidoluysian atrophy or DRPLA is sometimes included in the "
"group of autossomal dominant cerebellar ataxias type 1 because of its "
"various clinical combinations that are seen also in ADCA I diseases. DRPLA "
"is a disease believed to be mainly found in Japan."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:94
msgid "Spinal-bulbar muscular atrophy"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:95
msgid ""
"Spinal-bulbal muscular atrophy, also known as Kennedy disease, is a genetic "
"disorder where there is loss of motor neurons. SBMA is inherited in an X-"
"linked manner so carrier females have a 1/2 chance of transmitting the "
"mutation to each child."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:106
msgid ""
"Autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxias type 1 (ADCA I) is a group of diseases "
"that consists of cerebellar ataxia along with variable pyramidal, "
"extrapyramidal, and neuropathic signs. Four polyglutamine diseases are "
"included in this group: SCA1, SCA2, SCA3 and SCA17."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:117
msgid ""
"Autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxias type 2 is another ADCA group that "
"consists of diseases presented with cerebellar ataxia and retinal "
"degeneration. SCA7 is included in this group."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:127
msgid ""
"Autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxias type 3 is a group of diseases that "
"manifest pure cerebellar ataxia. Many spinocerebellar ataxias make this "
"group, but the one and only polyglutamine disease in this group is SCA6."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:147
msgid "Website briefing"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:149
msgid ""
"There are 9 polyglutamine diseases: Huntington's, SBMA, DRPLA, SCA1, SCA2, "
"SCA3, SCA6, SCA7 and\n"
"                    SCA17."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:152
msgid ""
"From brief disease introductions to molecular and biological mechanisms. "
"Here we present various\n"
"                    information about every polyglutmine disease to a "
"certain extent."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\home\index.html:155
msgid ""
"Each disease will have an introduction, first described cases description, \n"
"                    epidemiology data with representative maps, various "
"information on the gene that causes disease and the codified \n"
"                    protein (normal and mutated), pathophysiology section "
"which presents important cellular pathogenic mechanisms, a clinical \n"
"                    segment that includes neuropathology findings, signs and "
"symptoms found in disease patients and a final section regarding any \n"
"                    available active trials with experimental drugs and more."
msgstr ""

